  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF KERALA",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "c4mnoxx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient Kerala"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Kerala was ruled prominently by the Chera Dynasty, maintaining extensive maritime trade with Rome and Arabia.",
        "The arrival of Vasco da Gama at Kappad near Calicut in 1498 initiated European trade and colonial expansion in India.",
        "Travancore and Cochin developed as prominent princely states, with Marthanda Varma unifying Travancore.",
        "19th and 20th-century social reform movements fundamentally reshaped Kerala's socio-cultural environment.",
        "The state of Kerala was officially formed on November 1, 1956, merging Malabar, Cochin, and Travancore."
      ],
      "id": "twd12ab"
    },
    {
