    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vimyryf",
      "content": "Kerala's history stretches back to prehistoric times. The region was home to Neolithic cultures and later came under the influence of the Megalithic civilisation. The ancient name of Kerala was 'Keralaputra', mentioned in the Ashokan edicts of the 3rd century BCE."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xjcyaua",
      "content": "The Sangam Age (circa 300 BCE – 300 CE) is the golden era of ancient South Indian literature. During this period, the region was home to Chera dynasty who ruled the western coast. The Sangam literature — Purananuru, Akananuru, Padirruppattu — provides valuable historical insights about ancient Kerala."
    },
