      "content": "1.2 Medieval Kerala"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y0169kk",
      "content": "The medieval period saw the rise and fall of several kingdoms. The Kulashekhara dynasty (800–1102 CE) ruled Kerala and contributed immensely to Malayalam literature. Cheraman Perumal Nayanar, the last Kulashekhara king, is said to have converted to Islam and traveled to Mecca."
