    {
      "id": "9kmmkql",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.4 Travancore and Cochin"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a4i3ayo",
      "content": "Marthanda Varma (1706–1758) is considered the 'Maker of Modern Travancore'. He transformed Travancore from a weak kingdom into a powerful state. He defeated the Dutch at the Battle of Colachel (1741), the first Asian victory over a European power in modern warfare. His general Eustachius De Lannoy, the captured Dutch admiral, helped modernize the Travancore army."
    },
