    {
      "id": "whpx5oq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.7 Formation of Kerala State"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l6ialfl",
      "content": "Kerala was formed on November 1, 1956, when the States Reorganisation Act came into effect. The state was carved out of the former Travancore-Cochin state and the Malabar district of Madras State, uniting all Malayalam-speaking people under one administrative unit."
    },
